solghast-remnants-description = The Solghast Remnants are groups of surviving Solghans that were off-world or managed to evacuate from the planet before its destruction. They organize themselves into small groups or fleets with the same simple objectives, survival and the reformation of the Corporate Authority. They have yet to organize themselves in any meaningful way, with the remnants often coming to clash over who has the higher authority and overall distrust between themselves. Each remnant warband acts differently, with some resorting to piracy while others acting as first responders and peacekeepers, truly believing that the ends justify the means. The Solghan Corporate Authority was the name given to the short-lived polity based on the Solghan system, the Corporate Authority had declared independence from the Solarian Directive in the year 2820 after a series of events that they dubbed "The Great Separation". The Solghan state fought a war of attrition against the superior Solarian forces, although unable to secure the whole system they managed to inflict serious losses to the Solarians, for this the Solarian Directive decided to not attempt recapturing it and instead destroyed the planet after a decisive space battle. Prior to its destruction, Solghast had a population of around five billion. As Solghast society was a highly militarized one, it had a large military fleet to protect its assets. Most of the fleet was destroyed during the battle for the planet, but a large number of ships managed to disengage from the battle and escape. The corporation's CEOs had managed to establish highly effective operations, mainly in the mining industry, which gave the Authority a rather good economy. Native Solghans look human at first glance but are visually distinguished by their pale skin, frequent lack of hair, and imposing physical stature. Their bodies evolved to survive Solghan's extreme conditions over the course of many generations. They trace their origins to the humans who arrived to colonize the planet as part of a now unknown corporation's plan to establish new mining operations. The Solghan society has become highly revanchist, militarist, and isolationist. They believe that anything and everything should be done to reclaim their lost system and reestablish the Corporate Authority. But their main overall goal is survival. They are not above hiring mercenaries to complete their goals and are generally disinterested in the local affairs of the sector, mostly keeping to themselves or only doing things that would benefit them.